# FABLE-SONNET-OCC-ROOT-20260924-146: a repeated own-field occurrence under
# a NAMED (method) root, `test\[N]field`, resolved by the same occurrence
# lookup the rootless `\[N]field` form already uses (l2_own_find_occ) -- no
# second scanner.
#
# Measured (not assumed): an argument-bound field has no independent
# per-occurrence graph value. l2_emit_checkpoint publishes EVERY occurrence
# row of an argument-aliased field from the one canonical parameter cell
# (l2_p%d_%d), never from that row's own l2_q%d snapshot (the argument
# same-name-binding rule, L2 spec 18.3: "Its address and lifetime remain
# those of the parameter"). So test\[0]arg and test\[1]arg both read test's
# FINAL arg value once test has returned, same as unqualified test\arg --
# still a real, correctly-typed, non-crashing graph read reaching the right
# own row, just not distinguishing history for an argument specifically.
fn: test (int: arg) int
    arg: 1
    arg: 2
    return: 0
end: test

int: got
got: test(0)
if: test\[0]arg != 2
    return: 81
if: test\[1]arg != 2
    return: 82
if: test\arg != 2
    return: 83
return: 0
